# OmniSec Cursor AI Rules

## Project Identity
- **Name**: OmniSec (NetHunter Matrix v3.0)
- **Main controller**: `nhctl`
- **Source of truth**: `src/`
- **Generated artifacts**: `payload/` (`make stage`)
- **Build system**: `Makefile`
- **CI reference**: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
- **Language**: Bash (host), POSIX sh (device), C (native helpers), Python (AI/ML tools)

## Core Workflow
1. Read `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `AGENTS.md` first
2. Edit source files (`src/`, `scripts/`, `deploy/`, `tests/`)
3. Never edit generated artifacts (`payload/`, `build/`, `dist/`) unless explicitly asked
4. Run `make lint && make test` before concluding
5. Run `make stage` if source-to-payload files changed
6. Run `make validate` for deploy-impacting changes

## Code Conventions

### Host Scripts (Bash)
- Shebang: `#!/usr/bin/env bash`
- Strict mode: `set -euo pipefail`
- Source config: `. nh-defaults.sh`
- Color helpers: `say` (green), `warn` (yellow), `die` (red), `header` (cyan)
- Formatting: 4-space indent, 100-char ruler
- Functions: `snake_case`
- Variables: `UPPER_CASE` for constants, `lower_case` for locals
- Quote all variable expansions: `"$var"`

### Device Scripts (Android sh)
- Shebang: `#!/system/bin/sh`
- POSIX-compatible only (no bashisms)
- Minimal dependencies on external tools
- Use `nh-lib` for shared helpers

### C Code
- Standard: C17, static linking for helpers
- Flags: `-Wall -Wextra -pedantic`
- Naming: `snake_case`
- Avoid glibc-only assumptions (Android/Bionic compatibility)

### Python Code
- Format with Black
- Type hints preferred
- f-strings over concatenation

## Project Map
```
nhctl                    Host orchestration controller
src/device/bin/          Device-side nh-* tools (391 entries)
src/device/setup/        Setup/recovery scripts (15 files)
src/device/ai/           On-device AI agent (agent.py)
src/c/                   Native C helpers
src/device/dotfiles/     Termux dotfiles
deploy/magisk/           Magisk module packaging
deploy/android/          Android build props
scripts/                 Host automation scripts (33 files)
tests/                   BATS + C tests
kernel/                  Kernel build system
plugins/                 nh-* plugin ecosystem (161 files)
docs/                    Documentation
```

## Quality Gates
- `make lint` — Shell syntax, C syntax, JSON validation
- `make test` — BATS tests + C unit tests
- `make validate` — lint + test + validate.sh
- `make stage` — Stage src/ to payload/

## AI Agent Context Commands
- `make ai-cli-doctor` — Check AI CLI tool availability
- `make ai-context` — Generate repo context snapshot
- `make ai-bootstrap` — Standard workspace bootstrap
- `make ai-bootstrap-full` — Full workspace bootstrap

## Safety Rules
- No secrets, keys, or credentials in code
- No machine-specific paths
- Host scripts: Bash only
- Device scripts: Android `/system/bin/sh` only
- Prefer explicit failures over silent fallbacks
- Keep user-facing commands stable
- No refactoring unrelated files

## Memory Bank
This project uses a memory bank system for persistent AI context:
- `AGENTS.md` — Primary agent instructions
- `.github/copilot-instructions.md` — Copilot-specific instructions
- `.github/prompts/` — Workflow-specific prompt templates
- `.github/instructions/` — Scope-specific file instructions
- `ARCHITECTURE.md` — System architecture
- `docs/coding-standards.md` — Detailed coding standards
- `docs/priority.md` — Priority classification system
- `docs/security.md` — Security guidelines
- `docs/style-guide.md` — Output style guide
